# sent_id = beowulf.00002
# text = Oft Scyld Scēfing sceaþena þrēatum, monegum mǣgþum meodosetla oftēah, egsode eorl[as], syððan ǣrest wearð fēasceaft funden; hē þæs frōfre gebād, wēox under wolcnum weorðmyndum þāh, oð þæt him ǣghwylc ymbsittendra ofer hronrāde hȳran scolde, gomban gyldan; þæt wæs gōd cyning!
# ref = 4-11
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = Often Scyld Scefing took away the mead-benches from troops of enemies, from many peoples; he terrified the earls, after he was first found destitute. He experienced comfort for that, grew under the clouds, prospered in honors, until each of the neighboring peoples over the whale-road had to obey him and pay tribute. That was a good king!
# literal_translation = Often Scyld Scefing from-enemies' troops, from-many peoples, mead-benches took-away, terrified earls, after first was destitute found; he of-that comfort awaited, grew under clouds, in-honors throve, until to-him each of-neighbors over whale-road obey must, tribute pay; that was good king!
