# reading_translation = Wulfgar spoke — he was a man of the Wendels; his courage was made known to many, his warfare and wisdom —: 'I will ask the friend of the Danes, the lord of the Scyldings, the giver of rings, so as you are a petitioner, the famous prince about your journey, and quickly make known the answer to you, whether the good one intends to give it to me.'
# literal_translation = Wulfgar spoke -- that was of-Wendels a-man, was his mind-spirit to-many made-known, war and wisdom --: 'I of-that friend of-Danes, lord of-Scyldings to-ask will, of-rings giver, so as you petitioner are, prince famous about your journey, and to-you the answer quickly make-known, whether to-me the good-one to-give intends.'
