# sent_id = beowulf.00099
# text = Hǣbbe ic ēac geāhsod, þæt se ǣglǣca for his wonhȳdum wǣpna ne recceð; ic þæt þonne forhicge, swā mē Higelāc sīe, mīn mondrihten mōdes blīðe, þæt ic sweord bere oþðe sīdne scyld, geolorand tō gūþe, ac ic mid grāpe sceal fōn wið fēonde ond ymb feorh sacan, lāð wið lāþum; ðǣr gelȳfan sceal Dryhtnes dōme sē þe hine dēað nimerð.
# ref = 433-441
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = I have also heard that this monster, because of his reckless pride, does not care about weapons; then I will disdain that, so that my lord Hygelac may be glad at heart toward me, that I bear a sword or a broad shield, a yellow shield, to battle — but with my grip I must grapple with the foe and fight for life, hateful one against hateful one; there the one whom death takes must trust in the Lord's judgment.
# literal_translation = I-have also heard, that this monster for his reckless-prides weapons not cares; I that then despise, so that me Hygelac be, my liege-lord, of-mind glad, that I sword bear or broad shield, yellow-shield to battle, but I with grip shall seize against foe and about life contend, hateful against hateful; there trust shall Lord's judgment he who him death takes.
