# sent_id = beowulf.00147
# text = Ymbēode þā ides Helminga duguþe ond geogoþe dǣl ǣghwylcne, sincfato sealde, oþ þæt sǣl ālamp, þæt hīo Bēowulfe, bēaghroden cwēn mōde geþungen medoful ætbær; grētte Gēata lēod, Gode þancode wīsfæst wordum þæs ðe hire se willa gelamp, þæt hēo on ǣnigne eorl gelȳfde fyrena frōfre.
# ref = 620-628
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = Then the lady of the Helmings went about each of the seasoned warriors and the young, gave out treasure-vessels, until the time came that she, a ring-adorned queen, accomplished in heart, bore the mead-cup to Beowulf; she greeted the prince of the Geats, thanked God wisely in words that her wish had come to pass, that she could trust in any earl for comfort from crimes.
# literal_translation = Went-about then lady of-Helmings troop and youth each, treasure-vessels gave, until that time arrived, that she to-Beowulf, ring-adorned queen, in-mind accomplished, mead-cup bore; greeted Geats' prince, God thanked wise-firm in-words for-that which to-her the wish happened, that she in any earl trusted for-crimes' comfort.
