# reading_translation = For Sigemund, after his death-day, no little fame sprang up, after the hard warrior killed the dragon, the hoard's guardian; he, under the grey stone, the prince's son, alone dared the perilous deed — Fitela was not with him; nevertheless it befell him that the sword pierced through the wondrous dragon, so that it stood in the wall, the noble iron; the dragon died by the murder-blow.
