# sent_id = beowulf.00262
# text = Fin Hengeste elne unflitme āðum benemde, þæt hē þā wēalāfe weotena dōme ārum hēolde, þæt ðǣr ǣnig mon wordum nē worcum wǣre ne brǣce, nē þurh inwitsearo ǣfre gemǣnden, ðēah hīe hira bēaggyfan banan folgedon ðēodenlēase, þā him swā geþearfod wæs; gyf þonne Frȳsna hwylc frēcnan sprǣce ðæs morðorhetes myndgiend wǣre, þonne hit sweordes ecg sēðan scolde.
# ref = 1096-1106
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = Fin then declared to Hengest with valor and without dispute, by oaths, that he would hold the remnant of the survivors with the judgment of counselors and with honors, that there no man should break the agreement by words or deeds, nor ever mention it through treacherous cunning, though they, deprived of their lord, followed the slayer of their ring-giver, since it was so forced upon them; if then any one of the Frisians should be so bold as to bring up that murderous feud by reckless speech, then the sword's edge should settle it.
# literal_translation = Fin to-Hengest with-valor without-dispute by-oaths declared, that he the woeful-remnant of-counselors by-judgment with-honors should-hold, that there any man by-words nor by-deeds should-be nor break, nor through treacherous-cunning ever mention, though they their ring-giver's slayer followed lordless, when to-them so was-forced; if then of-Frisians any by-perilous speech of-the murderous-feud mindful should-be, then it sword's edge to-settle should.
