# text = þanon wōc fela geōsceaftgāsta; wæs þǣra Grendel sum, heorowearh hetelīc, sē æt Heorote fand wæccendne wer wīges bīdan; þǣer him āglǣca ætgrǣpe wearð; hwæþre hē gemunde mægenes strenge, gimfæste gife, ðē him God sealde, ond him tō Anwaldan āre gelȳfde, frōfre ond fultum; ðȳ hē þone fēond ofercwōm, gehnǣgde helle gāst.
# ref = 1265-1274
# source_version = perseus-ang1
# model = deepseek-chat
# reading_translation = From him sprang many monstrous spirits; one of them was Grendel, a hateful, hostile outcast, who at Heorot found a watchful man waiting for battle; there the monster came to grips with him; yet he remembered the strength of his might, the precious gift that God had given him, and he trusted in the Lord for mercy, comfort, and help; therefore he overcame the foe, humbled the spirit of hell.
# literal_translation = Thence woke many of-sorcerous-spirits; was of-them Grendel one, hostile-outcast hateful, he at Heorot found watchful man of-battle to-bide; there to-him the-monster in-grip became; yet he remembered of-might the-strength, gem-firm gift, that to-him God gave, and for-himself in the-Almighty grace believed, comfort and support; thereby he that foe overcame, humbled hell's spirit.
